# The mirror of combat-deathtouch-kills-regardless-of-toughness: there the
# ATTACKER had deathtouch; here the BLOCKER does. Craw Wurm (6/4, no
# keywords) attacks; Typhoid Rats (1/1, Deathtouch) blocks. dealPermanentDamage
# marks the deathtouch flag off whichever side dealt the damage, not off
# being the attacker specifically (combatdamage.go's own
# blk.HasKeyword("Deathtouch") check), so the Rats' single point of damage
# is lethal to the Wurm's 4 toughness regardless. The Wurm's 6 damage back
# is ordinary-lethal to the Rats' own 1 toughness regardless.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 2=1
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
advance
